<article class="env-lemma" id="0874">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0874">Lemma <span data-tag="0874">76.34.4</span>.</a> With notation and hypotheses as in Lemma <a href="/tag/082K" data-tag="082K">76.34.3</a>. Assume moreover that $f$ is locally of finite presentation. Then we can choose the factorization such that $T$ is finite and of finite presentation over $Y$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Limits of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/07VR" data-tag="07VR">70.11.3</a> we can write $T = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits T_ i$ where all $T_ i$ are finite and of finite presentation over $Y$ and the transition morphisms $T_{i'} \to T_ i$ are closed immersions. By Limits of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0827" data-tag="0827">70.5.7</a> there exists an $i$ and an open subscheme $U_ i \subset T_ i$ whose inverse image in $T$ is $X$. By Limits of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0828" data-tag="0828">70.5.12</a> we see that $X \cong U_ i$ for large enough $i$. Replacing $T$ by $T_ i$ finishes the proof. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>